    "year": 0,
    "content": "坊間常見「戒澱粉減肥法」。試從能量平衡與身體組成的角度分析此法的短期效果與長期問題，並說明體重秤上的數字為何會誤導。",
    "explanation": "本題須區分「體重下降」與「脂肪減少」兩件事。第三問是關鍵，要求解釋初期急速下降的成因。",
    "referenceAnswer": "短期效果：\n初期體重下降通常明顯而迅速，數日內可減二至三公斤。成因有三：\n一、糖原與水分流失。人體以糖原形式儲存碳水化合物，主要在肝臟與肌肉，總量約 400 至 500 克；而每 1 克糖原結合約 3 克水。戒澱粉後糖原耗盡，隨之釋出的水分經尿液排出，單此一項已可減 1.5 至 2 公斤 —— 全部並非脂肪。\n二、鈉與水分的連帶流失。碳水化合物攝取減少會影響腎臟對鈉的重吸收，進一步排出水分。\n三、總熱量下降。澱粉在多數人的飲食中佔比甚高，戒除之後若未以等量熱量的其他食物補足，實際上形成熱量赤字 —— 而真正令脂肪減少的是熱量赤字本身，不是「戒澱粉」這個動作。\n長期問題：\n一、可持續性低。極度限制某一類食物難以長期維持，一旦恢復進食澱粉，糖原與水分即時回補，體重迅速反彈，容易形成反覆循環並打擊信心。\n二、運動表現下降。高強度運動主要依靠糖解供能，糖原不足會令訓練質素下降，而肌肉量正是維持基礎代謝率的關鍵。\n三、營養素缺口。全穀類、豆類與水果同時提供膳食纖維、B 族維他命與礦物質，一併戒除可致纖維攝取不足與便秘。\n四、若熱量赤字過大且蛋白質攝取不足，流失的組織會包含肌肉。肌肉減少使基礎代謝率下降，其後維持同一體重所需的熱量更低，長遠反而更難控制體重。\n體重秤為何誤導：\n體重是身體所有成分的總和 —— 脂肪、肌肉、骨骼、水分、消化道內容物。其中水分佔體重約 50% 至 60%，且日內波動可達一至兩公斤，受飲水、鹽分、糖原、月經周期與排便影響。\n故短期內的體重變化主要反映水分，而非脂肪。一個人可以體重不變而脂肪減少、肌肉增加（身體組成改善）；亦可以體重下降而肌肉流失（身體組成惡化）。單一個數字無法分辨這兩種相反的情況。\n較可靠的做法：同時記錄腰圍、衣物合身度、體能表現與長期趨勢（以週或月為單位的平均值，而非逐日數字），並在條件許可時量度體脂率。",
    "marks": 1,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "Short-term effect: weight usually falls quickly at first, two or three kilograms within days, for three reasons.\nFirst, loss of glycogen and water. Carbohydrate is stored as glycogen, mainly in liver and muscle, totalling some 400 to 500 grams, and each gram of glycogen binds about three grams of water. When starch is cut, glycogen is depleted and the released water is passed as urine — 1.5 to 2 kilograms from this alone, none of it fat.\nSecond, associated loss of sodium and water, since lower carbohydrate intake affects renal sodium reabsorption.\nThird, a fall in total energy intake. Starch is a large share of most people's diet, and unless it is replaced with an equal number of calories, cutting it creates an energy deficit — and it is the deficit, not the act of avoiding starch, that reduces fat.\nLong-term problems: sustainability is poor, since severe restriction of one food group is hard to maintain, and when starch returns, glycogen and water are replaced at once and weight rebounds quickly, easily producing a repeated cycle that damages confidence. Exercise performance falls, because high-intensity work depends on glycolysis and low glycogen lowers training quality — and muscle mass is what maintains basal metabolic rate. Nutritional gaps appear, since wholegrains, pulses and fruit also supply fibre, B vitamins and minerals, and cutting them together can leave fibre intake too low, with constipation. And where the deficit is large and protein intake low, the tissue lost includes muscle; less muscle lowers basal metabolic rate, so fewer calories are needed to maintain the same weight and control becomes harder in the long run.\nWhy a scale misleads: body weight is the sum of everything in the body — fat, muscle, bone, water and the contents of the gut. Water is 50 to 60 per cent of body weight and can vary by one or two kilograms within a day with drinking, salt, glycogen, the menstrual cycle and bowel movements.\nShort-term changes in weight therefore reflect water rather than fat. A person may hold the same weight while losing fat and gaining muscle, an improvement in body composition, or lose weight while losing muscle, a deterioration. A single number cannot tell these opposite cases apart.\nMore reliable practice: record waist circumference, how clothes fit, physical performance and the long-run trend — weekly or monthly averages rather than daily figures — and measure body fat percentage where that is possible.",
    "contentEn": "Cutting out starch is a common approach to weight loss. Analyse its short-term effect and long-term problems in terms of energy balance and body composition, and explain why the reading on a scale can mislead.",
    "explanationEn": "The answer must distinguish weight loss from fat loss. The third part is the key and requires the cause of the rapid initial drop."
